  "id": "group-selection",
  "term": "group selection",
  "definition": "Group selection is natural selection acting on social groups rather than mainly on single individuals. In this sense, groups compete for survival and persistence, and individual success matters chiefly as it helps the group endure or prevail over other groups.",
